  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 7.45,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The ride from Ang Mo Kio to Raffles Place on the night of 18 July 2026 deviated from the platform's optimal route, and part of the fare is returned.\n\nThe route. The optimal route for this booking was 14.0 km (CTE southbound throughout, per the trip record's routing engine). The driver's GPS polyline measures 17.57 km, an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on the trace figure, which governs over the rounded 17.6 km copy. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (that needs over 50% or over 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged: no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral.\n\nThe GPS trace. I say two things about EV-GPS-00107. It is impaired at the schema level: admissibility weight 0.30, issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath jump on the final Raffles Place approach, implying 193.6 kph into and 238.9 kph out of the outlier). But it is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: there is no gap over 90 s (no gaps at all), the worst jump is 331.8 m (under the 500 m limb), and the sampling interval is a steady 10 s. So a deviation may be, and is, established on it, and the finding survives the 0.30 discount because it is independently carried.\n\nCorroboration. Because the rider's 60-day record shows 5 deviation claims with 1 substantiated, and the excess here is under 30%, POL-RD-08 requires corroboration beyond the GPS trace. It exists. The driver's own chat reply to the rider's challenge ('why exit at whitley?') -- 'cte very jam tonight boss' -- concedes that he left the CTE, and the driver's statement on file admits the route outright ('I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it'). Both are on the POL-RD-07(ii) list that POL-RD-08 borrows, and POL-RD-08 does not require the corroboration to re-measure the excess; a driver admission of the route is exactly what it names.\n\nThe driver's escalation argument. I do not accept that the 0.30 trace is the sole carrier of the deciding fact. The deviation is independently carried by the driver's chat admission on EV-CHAT-00107 (weight 1.0), so under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is the MAXIMUM of the independent carriers (1.0), not the minimum, and the 0.70 floor is not crossed. The counterparty statement is evidence and satisfies the corroboration limb, but it carries no weight and so does not itself set the cap.\n\nThe missing advisory. No traffic advisory was issued for the CTE that evening, so POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing and no closure-adjusted optimal can be built. The driver's 'it was jammed' is a general assertion unsupported by any advisory; under POL-RD-08 it does not discharge the burden of excusing the deviation, so the 3.57 km excess stands. That is a failure of the defence, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation: no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact (the driver's side expressly did not press POL-RD-03), and POL-RD-08 is the clause that governs an unsupported traffic assertion.\n\nOther points. POL-RD-04 does not apply: there was no rider instruction (waypoint_hint is null and no road is named), and the chat message was a challenge, not a request. POL-RD-11 does not apply: the fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-02 governs. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo discount. The 1.35 surge is a booking-time line applied to the recomputed optimal fare, not refunded as deviation damage.\n\nThe refund (POL-RD-02) is arithmetic. Charged total 36.60. Recomputed optimal-route fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 platform fee = (21.02 x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177. Refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and below 90% of the charged total, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 7.45. The charge is presently on the rider (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00); this order reverses SGD 7.45 of it."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The GPS impairment does not reach policy level. Under POL-RD-07 a trace is impaired for policy purposes only on a gap over 90 seconds, a straight-line jump over 500 m, or a sustained sampling interval over 30 seconds. This trace has no gaps at all (gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0.0), samples every 10 seconds, and its worst outlier jump is 331.8 m - under the 500 m limb. The deviation may therefore be established on the trace, and the pre-pass down-weighting of EV-GPS-00107 operates under POL-GEN-02 alone, which is a different question.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00107 at weight_multiplier 0.3 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No closure or advisory exoneration is available. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00107-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0: no congestion advisory was issued for the CTE on the evening of 18 July 2026, and the driver's assertion that CTE was jammed names no artifact. POL-RD-03 requires an advisory that names a road or segment the optimal route traverses and carries a validity window overlapping the pass; there is none, so no excess is exonerated and no closure-adjusted optimal route may be constructed.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00107-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The burden has shifted to the driver and he has not discharged it. POL-RD-08 requires the driver, once the rider has shown the excess, to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause to excuse it, and it states expressly that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge that burden. The driver's chat reply and his counterparty statement both assert a jam, but cite no advisory, and the advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is missing from the record. The 3.57 km excess therefore stands unexplained.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00107-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Escalation is not mandated on this record. The deciding facts are not carried by the 0.30 trace alone: the optimal distance the excess is measured against is carried by EV-TRIP-00107 at weight 1.0, and the route actually driven is independently admitted by the driver in EV-CHAT-00107 at weight 1.0. Under POL-GEN-02(2), where two or more independent artifacts carry the deciding fact the cap is the MAXIMUM of their weights rather than the minimum, so no POL-RD-10(1) confidence-floor trigger fires; and because the trace meets none of the POL-RD-07(a) to (c) limbs, POL-RD-10(3) does not fire either.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00107 at weight_multiplier 0.3 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED"
    }
  ]
}
